+## TL;DR
+- `AnythingLLM`, `Open WebUI`, and `Flowise` are strong general-purpose starting points for self-hosted AI knowledge management stacks.
+- `RAGFlow`, `Quivr`, and `MaxKB` are better fits when document ingestion, retrieval quality, and enterprise-style knowledge workflows matter most.
+- `Khoj`, `Reor`, `AFFiNE`, and `AppFlowy` are closer to personal or team knowledge management with notes, search, and AI-assisted recall.
+- `mem0`, `Zep`, `LightRAG`, and `KAG` are useful when you need memory, graph context, or retrieval infrastructure underneath an existing app.
+- Strictly pure-play open source AI knowledge management repos are still limited, so this list honestly includes adjacent RAG, memory, and document-AI projects that are commonly used to build KM systems.
