+# Contributing
+
+Thanks for contributing to this awesome list.
+
+## Submission Rules
+
+- Every submission must include a public `github.com` repository URL.
+- No proprietary SaaS products without a public GitHub repository.
+- Prefer projects with a clear open source license.
+- Include the current star count, primary language, license, and last commit date.
+- Base the description on the repository README or other repository-native documentation.
+- Explain why the project fits AI knowledge management, RAG, PKM, memory, search, or document understanding.
+
+## Pull Request Checklist
+
+- Confirm the repository is publicly accessible on GitHub.
+- Confirm the tool is relevant to AI knowledge management.
+- Confirm the license is stated in the repository.
+- Keep descriptions specific and neutral.
+- Update the Table of Contents if section structure changes.
+
+## Preferred Entry Format
+
+```md
+#### [Tool Name](https://github.com/username/repo)
+> **Description:** 80-150 words based on the GitHub README. Include last commit date, stars, primary language, and license.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/username/repo](https://github.com/username/repo)
+- **Stars:** 1234 ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** 2026-04-02
+- **Category:** tag1, tag2
+- **Best for:** specific use case
+```
+
+## Quality Bar
+
+Please do not submit:
+
+- Closed-source hosted products
+- Repositories without meaningful documentation
+- Abandoned repos with unclear relevance
+- Duplicate projects already represented in the list
+
+## License
+
+By contributing, you agree that your contributions will be licensed under the MIT License.
