+
+# Best AI Tools for Knowledge Management in 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-knowledge-management-2026?style=social)
+
+> This curated list covers the best AI tools for knowledge management in 2026 that you can inspect, fork, and self-host from public GitHub repositories. It focuses on open source RAG platforms, AI knowledge assistants, PKM apps with local-first workflows, memory layers, and document understanding stacks that help teams capture, retrieve, organize, and reuse knowledge without depending on proprietary SaaS.
+
+Snapshot reviewed: April 2, 2026. Repository stats and last-commit dates are best-effort GitHub snapshots and may move quickly.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `AnythingLLM`, `Open WebUI`, and `Flowise` are strong general-purpose starting points for self-hosted AI knowledge management stacks.
+- `RAGFlow`, `Quivr`, and `MaxKB` are better fits when document ingestion, retrieval quality, and enterprise-style knowledge workflows matter most.
+- `Khoj`, `Reor`, `AFFiNE`, and `AppFlowy` are closer to personal or team knowledge management with notes, search, and AI-assisted recall.
+- `mem0`, `Zep`, `LightRAG`, and `KAG` are useful when you need memory, graph context, or retrieval infrastructure underneath an existing app.
+- Strictly pure-play open source AI knowledge management repos are still limited, so this list honestly includes adjacent RAG, memory, and document-AI projects that are commonly used to build KM systems.
+
+## Why This List
+The best AI tools for knowledge management are increasingly open source because teams want control over embeddings, documents, prompts, private data, model choice, and hosting costs. GitHub-native projects also make it easier to audit licenses, review community activity, and adapt a stack for internal wikis, research libraries, customer support knowledge bases, and personal knowledge management workflows.
+
